{"id":"dc5366796483404a","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-df-stable.md","title":"Stable","display":"df-stable — Stable","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-stable","aliases":["58-df-stable","Stable"],"display":"df-stable — Stable","depends_on":["[[58-df-metric-space]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-stable"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-stable</span><span>Stable</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-stable — Stable"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"58-df-metric-space\">58-df-metric-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(X,d)\">\\((X,d)\\)</span> (metric state space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Phi:[0,\\infty)\\times X\\to X\">\\(\\Phi:[0,\\infty)\\times X\\to X\\)</span> (semiflow)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x^*\\in X\">\\(x^*\\in X\\)</span> (equilibrium candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\)</span> (metric-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"58-df-metric-space\">58-df-metric-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Semiflow}_S,\\mathrm{FlowEquilibrium}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Semiflow}_S,\\mathrm{FlowEquilibrium}_S\\)</span> (predicates defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{LyapunovStable}_S,\\operatorname{AsymptoticallyStable}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{LyapunovStable}_S,\\operatorname{AsymptoticallyStable}_S\\)</span> (stability predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable} \\vdash \\mathrm{Semiflow}_S(\\Phi,X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(\\Phi,[0,\\infty)\\times X,X)\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\Phi(0,x)=x)\\land\\forall s,t\\ge0\\;\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\Phi(s+t,x)=\\Phi(s,\\Phi(t,x)))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable} \\vdash \\mathrm{Semiflow}_S(\\Phi,X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(\\Phi,[0,\\infty)\\times X,X)\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\Phi(0,x)=x)\\land\\forall s,t\\ge0\\;\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\Phi(s+t,x)=\\Phi(s,\\Phi(t,x)))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}equilibrium} \\vdash \\mathrm{FlowEquilibrium}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Semiflow}_S(\\Phi,X)\\land x^*\\in X\\land\\forall t\\in[0,\\infty)\\;(\\Phi(t,x^*)=x^*)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}equilibrium} \\vdash \\mathrm{FlowEquilibrium}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Semiflow}_S(\\Phi,X)\\land x^*\\in X\\land\\forall t\\in[0,\\infty)\\;(\\Phi(t,x^*)=x^*)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}lyapunov} \\vdash \\operatorname{LyapunovStable}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X,d)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\mathrm{FlowEquilibrium}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X)\\land\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall x_0\\in X\\;\\forall t\\in[0,\\infty)\\;(d(x_0,x^*)&lt;\\delta\\to d(\\Phi(t,x_0),x^*)&lt;\\varepsilon)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}lyapunov} \\vdash \\operatorname{LyapunovStable}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X,d)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\mathrm{FlowEquilibrium}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X)\\land\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall x_0\\in X\\;\\forall t\\in[0,\\infty)\\;(d(x_0,x^*)&lt;\\delta\\to d(\\Phi(t,x_0),x^*)&lt;\\varepsilon)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}asymptotic} \\vdash \\operatorname{AsymptoticallyStable}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X,d)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{LyapunovStable}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X,d)\\land\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall x_0\\in X\\;\\bigl(d(x_0,x^*)&lt;\\delta\\to\\lim_{t\\to\\infty}d(\\Phi(t,x_0),x^*)=0\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}asymptotic} \\vdash \\operatorname{AsymptoticallyStable}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X,d)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{LyapunovStable}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X,d)\\land\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall x_0\\in X\\;\\bigl(d(x_0,x^*)&lt;\\delta\\to\\lim_{t\\to\\infty}d(\\Phi(t,x_0),x^*)=0\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Lyapunov stability means nearby trajectories remain nearby; asymptotic stability additionally requires local attraction.</li>\n<li>For the linear flow <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\dot x=Ax\">\\(\\dot x=Ax\\)</span>, the origin is asymptotically stable exactly when <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> is Hurwitz.</li>\n<li>A positive-definite Lyapunov function with negative-semidefinite derivative gives stability; a negative-definite derivative gives asymptotic stability under the standard regularity hypotheses.</li>\n<li>Center manifold: non-hyperbolic eigenvalues require center manifold reduction</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Perko, Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems</li>\n<li>Chicone, Ordinary Differential Equations with Applications</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-metric-space","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-metric-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-metric-space","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)$ (metric-space predicate, see [[58-df-metric-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}$ (function predicate, see [[58-df-function]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(X,d)","display":false},{"tex":"\\Phi:[0,\\infty)\\times X\\to X","display":false},{"tex":"x^*\\in X","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Semiflow}_S,\\mathrm{FlowEquilibrium}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{LyapunovStable}_S,\\operatorname{AsymptoticallyStable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable} \\vdash \\mathrm{Semiflow}_S(\\Phi,X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(\\Phi,[0,\\infty)\\times X,X)\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\Phi(0,x)=x)\\land\\forall s,t\\ge0\\;\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\Phi(s+t,x)=\\Phi(s,\\Phi(t,x)))","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}equilibrium} \\vdash \\mathrm{FlowEquilibrium}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Semiflow}_S(\\Phi,X)\\land x^*\\in X\\land\\forall t\\in[0,\\infty)\\;(\\Phi(t,x^*)=x^*)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}lyapunov} \\vdash \\operatorname{LyapunovStable}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X,d)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\mathrm{FlowEquilibrium}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X)\\land\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall x_0\\in X\\;\\forall t\\in[0,\\infty)\\;(d(x_0,x^*)<\\delta\\to d(\\Phi(t,x_0),x^*)<\\varepsilon)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}stable\\text{-}asymptotic} \\vdash \\operatorname{AsymptoticallyStable}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X,d)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{LyapunovStable}_S(\\Phi,x^*,X,d)\\land\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall x_0\\in X\\;\\bigl(d(x_0,x^*)<\\delta\\to\\lim_{t\\to\\infty}d(\\Phi(t,x_0),x^*)=0\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\dot x=Ax","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false}],"bytes":2462,"backlinks":[{"id":"e0e3f6d67f68f8d4","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{LyapunovStable}_S(\\Phi,x_0,X,d)$ (Lyapunov-stability predicate, see [[../batch16/58-df-stable.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1218","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-stable.md|58-df-stable]]（batch16）"}],"outgoing":["ce876585d129ce97","36d7463d215be751"]}